From cb53cae9bd43c4eab09cdbdf8f8dc4e3aab72b95 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 23:28:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Gate Purchase Navigator checkout behind a pre-payment
 sufficiency check
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Fixes a bait-and-switch flow found in QA: a customer could pay $19 with
a vague query like "fridge purchase 33 inch" and only learn afterward,
via the AI's own honest response, that there wasn't enough information
to produce the promised total-cost-of-ownership report. The only
pre-payment check was "is the description box non-empty" (client and
server), and nothing verified the input could actually support the six
things the page promises to deliver.

- navigator-buying-rules.js: isomorphic (browser + Node) definition of
  "enough information" per purchase category (vehicle/appliance/other),
  with a human-readable reason for every required field.
- buying.html: category picker + dynamic, tailored, explained fields;
  checkout stays disabled with an inline explanation of what's missing
  until sufficiency is met, then shows a confirmation of exactly what
  will be analyzed and delivered before payment.
- api/navigator-intake.js: enforces the same check server-side for the
  'buying' product so the frontend gate can't be bypassed by calling the
  API directly. Other 12 products' existing behavior is untouched.
- api/_lib/purchase-engine.js: new dedicated report engine with a schema
  that requires all six promised sections to be non-empty (verified in
  code, not just implied by a prompt), retries on an incomplete
  response, optionally grounds figures via Anthropic's web_search tool
  with a graceful knowledge-only fallback, and maps into the existing
  generic report shape so navigator-status.html needed no changes.
- api/get-navigator-submission.js: routes 'buying' to the new engine,
  mirroring the existing 'contractor' special case.
- navigator-status.html: buying-specific failure copy states the
  retry/refund policy explicitly.
- tests/: node:test coverage for the sufficiency rules (vague vs.
  sufficient input per category), server-side gating (mocked Supabase),
  and the engine's completeness guarantee, retry behavior, and
  web-search fallback (mocked fetch + Supabase) — 25 tests, no network
  or live credentials required.

